    "created_at": "2021-04-29T22:44:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-29T22:44:38Z",
    "body": "> The proposal is almost same as [`<menuitem>`](https://www.w3.org/TR/html51/interactive-elements.html#the-menuitem-element), which we removed from the specification.\r\n> Blink team's stance is that we should not provide complex UI features, and should provide primitives to help implementing such UI features instead.\r\n\r\nI believe that allowing arbitrary HTML within `<option>` elements (both for `<select>` and `<datalist>`) would be inline with the goal of providing \"_primitives to help implementing such UI features_\". The alternative at this time is a custom form control, which is generally harmful for the web.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
